	(text "J5 has the pin order of the PPK2 logic port: 1 VCC, 2 ground, 3 to 10 are D7 to D0.\nU36, U37 and U35 clamp D0 to D7 and the VCC pin to ground (5.5 V working voltage).\nRN8 / RN9 limit the input current and keep the edge slope at U38 inside its limit\n(calculated 2.6 to 3.3 ns/V at 5 V against 5 ns/V). RN11 / RN10 hold an open input\nlow for a pin leakage up to 1 uA, the 25 C limit of the datasheet. A line held high\nloads the DUT with V / 470 k: 3.5 uA at 1.65 V, 7 uA at 3.3 V, 10.6 uA at 5 V.\nDIR and OE are tied low: enabled, direction B to A. With port B unpowered the outputs\nfloat; pull-downs on the Side Data sheet hold DIN0 to DIN7."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 78.74 168.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "37c21a13-953c-53a3-8d72-ffd4ab617cd9")
	)
	(text "Supply of port B of U38: 1.65 V to 5.5 V in use, limits -0.5 V and 6.5 V (datasheet).\nJP2 bridged 1-2 as built: the supply is VCCB_SRC, the guard buffer output behind 1 k on\nthe Output Stage sheet, so the logic thresholds follow the DUT supply.\nD24 holds that node between ground and +5 V for every state of the buffer:\nsimulated -0.40 V and +5.4 V with +5 V at 5.0 V (0 C and 27 C); calculated 6.0 V at 5.61 V.\nJP2 cut 1-2 and bridged 2-3: the supply is the VCC pin of the port through R139,\nfor a DUT whose logic runs on another voltage than its supply. Cut 1-2 before bridging 2-3.\nC100 and C101 decouple the two supply pins of U38 and sit at pins 23 / 24 and 1.\nTP48: VCC_B as the translator sees it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.84 16.51 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3fbcb7cd-bffd-5903-a02a-f6a078c3ec19")
	)
